<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Contributors at the Confused Catholic"
	pubDate={new Date('April 26 2026')}
>
	<h4>Jake Nulty</h4>
	<p>
		By trade, I'm a technical writer. Before that, I was a butcher from 2010-2023. I was born and raised Catholic.
		In my teenage years, I left the Church. I did not return for almost two decades. When returning to the Church,
		I discovered that many online sources claim to be Catholic yet teach things completely contrary to Catholic teaching.
	</p>
	<p>
		Before returning, I joined a "Bible in a year" study group at the <a href="https://discord.gg/uaSMGsDtFJ">
		Love First Christians Discord channel</a>. As a teenager, we did some Bible study when preparing for Confirmation
		but never anything this extensive. Halfway through Leviticus, I began to long for the Liturgical depth
		I took for granted as a young man. By the time I started reading Samuel, I couldn't keep lying to myself -- I was still
		Catholic and I never really stopped being Catholic. I just stopped practicing. On Palm Sunday of 2025, my family returned
		to the Catholic Church. I began documenting my experiences returning to Church and started <a href="https://theconfusedcatholic.substack.com/">
		the Confused Catholic Substack</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
